sequenceDiagram
    actor Client
    actor MCPClient as MCP Client
    participant API as graphify-api
    participant NATS as NATS JetStream
    participant MemWorker as graphify-memoryworker
    participant FS as data/memories (shared vol)
    participant MCP as graphify-mcp (Python)

    Client->>API: POST /api/v1/memories {name, description}
    API-->>Client: 201 {memoryId}

    loop For each source: git repo or uploaded file
        Client->>API: POST /api/v1/memories/:memId/resources {url or upload}
        API->>FS: Store.Create resource(status=queued)
        API->>NATS: publish memory.resource.requested (MsgId: mem-resource:memId:resId)
        API-->>Client: 202 {resourceId}

        NATS->>MemWorker: deliver memory.resource.requested  [durable: resource-workers-v1]

        alt git resource
            MemWorker->>FS: IngestGit: git clone --depth 1 then graphify extract
            FS-->>MemWorker: graphify-out/graph.json per resource
        else file resource (PDF / docx / md)
            MemWorker->>FS: IngestFile: graphify extract (detect + convert)
            FS-->>MemWorker: graphify-out/graph.json per resource
        end

        MemWorker->>FS: Store.Update resource(status=ready, relPath, graphOutPath)
        MemWorker->>NATS: publish memory.resource.ready (MsgId: mem-resource-ready:memId:resId)
    end

    note over NATS,MemWorker: when all resources are ready auto-trigger merge
    NATS->>MemWorker: deliver memory.merge.requested  [durable: merge-workers-v1]

    MemWorker->>FS: Assemble: stage each resource graph into labelled dir resourceLabel/graphify-out/graph.json
    MemWorker->>FS: graphify merge-graphs inputs to graphify-out/graph.json (cross-source tags via grandparent dir)
    MemWorker->>FS: Correlate: add hub nodes for shared packages, add cross-source links
    MemWorker->>FS: graphify enrich best-effort graph.html GRAPH_REPORT.md graphml svg
    MemWorker->>FS: git commit graphify-out/ and memory.json
    FS-->>MemWorker: GraphRef = HEAD SHA
    MemWorker->>FS: Store.Update memory(status=ready, graphRef=SHA, artifacts)
    MemWorker->>NATS: publish memory.merge.ready (MsgId: mem-merge-ready:memId:sha)

    Client->>API: GET /api/v1/memories/:memId
    API-->>Client: {status=ready, graphRef, artifacts[]}

    note over MCPClient,MCP: MCP query surface for vionix-engram integration tests
    MCPClient->>MCP: docker run graphify-service -v graph.json:/graphify-service/repos/graph.json
    note over MCP: python -m graphify.serve --transport http --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080 --stateless --json-response /graphify-service/repos/graph.json
    MCPClient->>MCP: HTTP POST /mcp  CallTool query_memory
    MCPClient->>MCP: {query: what version of react is used in this project?}
    MCP->>MCP: LLM reasoning over graph.json nodes and edges
    MCP-->>MCPClient: react@18.2.0 declared as dependency in package.json
